        "inherited_unit:005.paragraph"
      ],
      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Slides FOSS for Java reads and writes Office Open XML presentation files (.pptx), builds the Office Open XML package itself, so it needs no PowerPoint installation, no native code, and no runtime dependencies at all — the CycloneDX SBOM the build produces lists zero components."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:002",
        "example:003",
        "example:004",
        "example:005",
        "example:006",
        "example:008",
        "example:010",
        "example:011",
        "example:012"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "It creates and edits presentations by instantiating the Presentation class, adding or removing slides via SlideCollection methods, and saving to PPTX, PPSX, or POTX formats using save methods."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:002",
        "example:012"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "It adds and formats shapes by inserting AutoShapes, PictureFrames, Tables, and Connectors through ShapeCollection methods, then configuring their fill, line, and geometry properties."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:011"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "It formats text content by setting font height, bold, fill color, and other character attributes at the Portion level, paragraph alignment and bullets at the Paragraph level, and text frame margins and autofit at the TextFrame level."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:005"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "It applies visual effects such as outer shadow, inner shadow, glow, soft edge, reflection, blur, preset shadow, and fill overlay to shapes via EffectFormat methods."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "example:006"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "It manages comments and notes by adding comment authors and threaded comments with timestamps and positions, and by creating speaker notes per slide through NotesSlideManager."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:002",
        "example:003",
        "example:004",
        "example:005",
        "example:006",
        "example:008",
        "example:010",
        "example:011",
        "example:012"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "It embeds images by loading them from bytes, files, or streams into the ImageCollection and attaching them to slides as PictureFrames."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:008"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:7",
      "text": "It clones and manages slides by duplicating existing slides with addClone, inserting empty slides, removing slides by index, and controlling slideshow visibility with setHidden."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:004"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:8",
      "text": "It sets document properties such as title, subject, author, keywords, category, and custom values through the IDocumentProperties interface."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001"
      ],
      "section": "quick_start",
      "slot": "lead_in",
      "text": "This example creates a new presentation, clears the first slide, adds a solid blue rectangle shape, and saves it as a PPTX file named hello.pptx."
    },
