        "public_symbol:org.aspose",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose.slides"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "intro",
      "text": "The primary entry point is Presentation, which owns an ISlideCollection of Slide objects; each slide exposes an IShapeCollection of Shape-derived objects (AutoShape, Connector, Table, PictureFrame) built through ShapeCollection's addAutoShape(), addConnector(), addTable(), and addPictureFrame() methods. The org.aspose.slides package hosts these core classes."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:org",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose.slides"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:org.aspose",
      "text": "The org.aspose package serves as the top-level namespace for Aspose.Slides FOSS for Java, under which the org.aspose.slides subpackage provides the presentation processing API."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:org",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose.slides"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:org.aspose.slides",
      "text": "The org.aspose.slides package contains the core classes for working with presentations, including Presentation, Slide, Shape, and their associated collections and formatting interfaces."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:org",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose",
        "public_symbol:org.aspose.slides"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:org",
      "text": "The org package is the root namespace for Java libraries, and org.aspose is the top-level package for Aspose products."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:relationship"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:relationship",
      "text": "The Relationship class represents a relationship between parts in a presentation package, typically used when working with Open Packaging Conventions."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:getfontname"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:getfontname",
      "text": "The getFontName method retrieves the name of a font used in a text portion or format."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
